{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789384463,"nonce":"g1kS0AgvZJOzGvoYtInS1HypP4Y=","title":"Python: a method's instance parameter is null-checked at every read, and the caller checks for a raise after every call","message":"After nullable instances (c83326a), `def __add__(self, other)` with\n`other` inferred `Vec3` checks `other` for None before `other.x`, so\nthe method may raise AttributeError, so every `acc + a` is followed by\na pending-exception check, and the result merges with a null from the\nraise path. Against ZynML's same kernel that is: two pending checks, a\nnull check per operand, a phi with a null incoming that stops\n`scalar_replace_alloc` from removing the intermediate `acc + a` (ZynML\nallocates once per iteration, ZyPy twice), and a raising callee that\ncannot be a non-raising one. op_overload ran 125 ms to ZynML's 84.\n\nThree pieces, all deciding at compile time what is already known:\n\n1. Always-instance locals (`Lowerer::always_instances`): a variable\n   first mentioned by a top-level `x = C(...)` and assigned nothing\n   else anywhere in the body holds an instance throughout, so `a` in\n   `for ...: acc = acc + a` needs no check inside the loop.\n2. Trusted variants: an item with an instance-typed parameter is\n   lowered twice, the second as `name$trusted` with those parameters\n   taken to be instances. A call whose every such argument is known to\n   be one (`call_target`) goes to the variant, which the raise analysis\n   sees separately, so `__add__$trusted` is non-raising and its\n   callers skip the pending check. Dynamic hooks and dispatchers keep\n   calling the checked one.\n3. Never-None results (`types::returning_instances`): an item every\n   `return` of which hands back a constructor call, `self`, or another\n   such item's result, and whose body cannot fall off its end, returns\n   an instance, so `acc = acc + a` keeps `acc` known.\n\nAnd, separately, a field settled by a test: `if self.left is None:\nreturn` leaves `self.left` known for the rest of the block (until a\ncall or a store to that field), and `if x is not None:` inside its\nbody; `Lowerer::nonnull_fields`.\n\nop_overload 125 to 63.6 ms (with 1e74bd8), the loop one block with\none allocation like ZynML's; op_overload_ref 13.3 to 7.1;\nbinary_trees 331 to 269 (ZynML 212: the remaining gap is the pending\ncheck after each recursive `check` and the null check of `self.right`\nafter the call). Conformance `class/instance_arguments.py`.","files":null}]}